<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Tunbyholm_Castle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Tunbyholm Castle (Swedish: Tunbyholms slott) is a manor house at Tomelilla Municipality in Scania, Sweden. The facility consists of a two-story building with yellow facades, white pilasters and window surrounds as well as two free-standing wings with square floors, flat saddle roof and pediment-crowned central section. The present appearance is the result of a classic restoration in the 1830s."@en .
