<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ponce,_Puerto_Rico> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Ponce** (, , Template:IPA-es, Template:IPA-es) is both a [city](:City) and a [municipality](:Municipalities_of_Puerto_Rico) on the southern coast of [Puerto Rico](:Puerto_Rico). The city is the seat of the municipal government.Ponce, Puerto Rico's most populated city outside the [San Juan](:San_Juan%2C_Puerto_Rico) metropolitan area, was founded on 12 August 1692 and is named for [Juan Ponce de León y Loayza](:Juan_Ponce_de_Le%C3%B3n_y_Loayza), the great-grandson of Spanish conquistador [Juan Ponce de León](:Juan_Ponce_de_Le%C3%B3n). Ponce is often referred to as *La Perla del Sur* (The Pearl of the South), *La Ciudad Señorial* (The Manorial City), and *La Ciudad de las Quenepas* ([Genip](:Genip) City). The city serves as the governmental seat of the autonomous municipality as well as the regional hub for various [Government of Puerto Rico](:Government_of_Puerto_Rico) entities, such as the [Judiciary of Puerto Rico](:Supreme_Court_of_Puerto_Rico). It is also the regional center for various other Government of Puerto Rico and [US Federal Government](:Federal_government_of_the_United_States) agencies. Ponce is a principal city of both the [Ponce Metropolitan Statistical Area](:Ponce_metropolitan_area) and the [Ponce-Yauco-Coamo Combined Statistical Area](:Ponce_metropolitan_area%23Combined_Statistical_Area).The [Municipality of Ponce](:Municipalities_of_Puerto_Rico), officially the *Autonomous Municipality of Ponce*, is located in the southern coastal plain region of the island, south of [Adjuntas](:Adjuntas%2C_Puerto_Rico), [Utuado](:Utuado%2C_Puerto_Rico), and [Jayuya](:Jayuya%2C_Puerto_Rico); east of [Peñuelas](:Pe%C3%B1uelas%2C_Puerto_Rico); west of [Juana Díaz](:Juana_D%C3%ADaz%2C_Puerto_Rico); and bordered on the south by the [Caribbean Sea](:Caribbean_Sea). The municipality has 31 [barrios](:Barrio), including 19 outside the city's urban area and 12 in the urban area of the city. The historic *[Ponce Pueblo](:Ponce_Historic_Zone)* district, located in the downtown area of the city, is shared by several of the downtown barrios, and is located approximately three miles (4.8 km) inland from the shores of the Caribbean. The municipality of Ponce is the second largest in Puerto Rico by land area, and it was the first in Puerto Rico to obtain its [autonomy](:Self-governance), becoming the *Autonomous Municipality of Ponce* in 1992."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
