<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bayamón,_Puerto_Rico> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Bayamón (Spanish pronunciation: [baʝaˈmon]) is a city, municipality of Puerto Rico and suburb of San Juan located in the northern coastal valley, north of Aguas Buenas and Comerío; south of Toa Baja and Cataño; west of Guaynabo; and east of Toa Alta and Naranjito. Bayamón is spread over 11 barrios and Bayamón Pueblo (the downtown area and the administrative center of the city). It is part of the San Juan-Caguas-Guaynabo Metropolitan Statistical Area and the second most populous municipality in both the metropolitan area and Puerto Rico."@en .
