<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Town_hall> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "In local government, a city hall, town hall, civic centre (in the UK or Australia), guildhall, or a municipal building (in the Philippines), is the chief administrative building of a city, town, or other municipality. It usually houses the city or town council, its associated departments, and their employees. It also usually functions as the base of the mayor of a city, town, borough, county or shire, and of the executive arm of the municipality (if one exists distinctly from the council). Other terms in non-English languages are Mairie or Hôtel de ville (France) or Maison communale (Belgium), Gemeindehaus or Rathaus (Germany), Municipio (Italy), Rådhus (Denmark), Paços do Concelho (Portugal), Gemeentehuis or Stadhuis (The Netherlands and Belgium) and Stadshus (Sweden)."@en .
