<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Cazenovia,_New_York> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Cazenovia is a town in Madison County, New York. The population was 6,740 at the time of the 2020 census. The town is named after Theophilus Cazenove, an agent of the Holland Land Company. The Town of Cazenovia has a village also named Cazenovia. The town is on the county's western border. The village of Cazenovia is home to Cazenovia College, a small liberal arts college in the greater Syracuse area. It was founded in 1824, known then as the Genesee Seminary."@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Arena_Sozopol> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Arena Sozopol is a football stadium in Sozopol, Bulgaria, with a seating capacity of 3,500. It has been the home of FC Sozopol since 2012, and hosted 8 games during the 2015 UEFA European Under-17 Championship, with an average attendance of 1,395 per game (11,154 in total)."@en .
