<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bayamón,_Puerto_Rico> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Bayamón** (Template:IPA-es, Template:IPA-es) is a [city](:Bayam%C3%B3n_barrio-pueblo), [municipality](:Municipalities_of_Puerto_Rico) of [Puerto Rico](:Puerto_Rico) and suburb of [San Juan](:San_Juan%2C_Puerto_Rico) located in the northern coastal valley, north of [Aguas Buenas](:Aguas_Buenas%2C_Puerto_Rico) and [Comerío](:Comer%C3%ADo%2C_Puerto_Rico); south of [Toa Baja](:Toa_Baja%2C_Puerto_Rico) and [Cataño](:Cata%C3%B1o%2C_Puerto_Rico); west of [Guaynabo](:Guaynabo%2C_Puerto_Rico); and east of [Toa Alta](:Toa_Alta%2C_Puerto_Rico) and [Naranjito](:Naranjito%2C_Puerto_Rico). Bayamón is spread over 11 [barrios](:Ward_%28country_subdivision%29) and [Bayamón Pueblo](:Bayam%C3%B3n_barrio-pueblo) (the [downtown](:Downtown) area and the [administrative center](:Administrative_center) of the city). It is part of the [San Juan-Caguas-Guaynabo Metropolitan Statistical Area](:San_Juan-Caguas-Guaynabo_Metropolitan_Statistical_Area) and the second most populous municipality in both the metropolitan area and Puerto Rico."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
