<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Gulen_Church> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Gulen Church** (Template:Lang-no is a [parish church](:Parish_church) of the [Church of Norway](:Church_of_Norway) in [Gulen Municipality](:Gulen_Municipality) in [Vestland](:Vestland) county, [Norway](:Norway). It is located in the village of [Eivindvik](:Eivindvik). It is the church for the Gulen [parish](:Parish) which is part of the [Nordhordland prosti](:Nordhordland_prosti) ([deanery](:Deanery%29) in the [Diocese of Bjørgvin](:Diocese_of_Bj%C3%B8rgvin). The white, wooden church was built in a [long church](:Long_church) design in 1863 using plans drawn up by the [architect](:Architect) [Georg Andreas Bull](:Georg_Andreas_Bull). The church seats about 700 people. The church stands on a hill in central [Eivindvik](:Eivindvik), with magnificent views towards the [Gulafjorden](:Gulafjorden)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
