<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Nevada,_Iowa> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Nevada** ( [*nə-VAY-də*](:Help%3APronunciation_respelling_key%29) is a city in, and the [county seat](:County_seat) of, [Story County](:Story_County%2C_Iowa), [Iowa](:Iowa), United States. The population was 6,925 in the [2020 census](:2020_United_States_Census), an increase from 6,658 in [2000](:2000_United_States_Census). Nevada is part of the [Ames, Iowa](:Ames%2C_Iowa) [Metropolitan Statistical Area](:Metropolitan_Statistical_Area), which is a part of the larger Ames-[Boone, Iowa](:Boone%2C_Iowa) [Combined Statistical Area](:Combined_Statistical_Area). Nevada is the second-most populous city in [Story County](:Story_County%2C_Iowa). The city's name is pronounced differently from the U.S. state of [Nevada](:Nevada)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
