<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Massachusetts> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Massachusetts (Massachusett: Muhsachuweesee [məhsatʃəwiːsi:], English: /ˌmæsəˈtʃuːsɪts/, /-zɪts/), officially the Commonwealth of Massachusetts, is the most populous state in the New England region of the Northeastern United States. It borders on the Atlantic Ocean and Gulf of Maine to the east, Connecticut and Rhode Island to the south, New Hampshire and Vermont to the north, and New York to the west. The state's capital and most populous city, as well as its cultural and financial center, is Boston. Massachusetts is also home to the urban core of Greater Boston, the largest metropolitan area in New England and a region profoundly influential upon American history, academia, and the research economy. Originally dependent on agriculture, fishing, and trade. Massachusetts was transformed"@en .
