<http://dbpedia.org/resource/St_Pancras_Renaissance_London_Hotel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The St. Pancras Renaissance London Hotel forms the frontispiece of St Pancras railway station, one of the main termini in London and the final stop for international trains departing to Paris, Brussels, Amsterdam and other destinations in mainland Europe. It opened in 2011, and occupies much of the former Midland Grand Hotel designed by George Gilbert Scott which opened in 1873 and closed in 1935. The hotel is managed by Marriot International. The hotel is located in the vicinity of Euston, King's Cross and St Pancras railway stations."@en .
