<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Toyota> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Toyota Motor Corporation** ([Japanese](:Japanese_language): トヨタ自動車株式会社, [Hepburn](:Hepburn_romanization): *Toyota Jidōsha kabushikigaisha*, Template:IPA-ja, , commonly known as simply **Toyota**) is a Japanese [multinational](:Multinational_corporation) [automotive](:Automotive_industry) manufacturer headquartered in [Toyota City, Aichi](:Toyota_City%2C_Aichi), Japan. It was founded by [Kiichiro Toyoda](:Kiichiro_Toyoda) and incorporated on August 28, 1937 (1937-08-28). Toyota is one of the [largest automobile manufacturers](:Automotive_industry%23By_manufacturer) in the world, producing about 10 million vehicles per year.The company was originally founded as a spinoff of [Toyota Industries](:Toyota_Industries), a machine maker started by [Sakichi Toyoda](:Sakichi_Toyoda), Kiichiro's father. Both companies are now part of the [Toyota Group](:Toyota_Group), one of the largest conglomerates in the world. While still a department of Toyota Industries, the company developed its first product, the [Type A engine](:Toyota_Type_A_engine) in 1934 and its first passenger car in 1936, the [Toyota AA](:Toyota_AA).After World War II, Toyota benefited from Japan's alliance with the United States to learn from American automakers and other companies, which would give rise to [The Toyota Way](:The_Toyota_Way) (a management philosophy) and the [Toyota Production System](:Toyota_Production_System) (a [lean manufacturing](:Lean_manufacturing) practice) that would transform the small company into a leader in the industry and would be the subject of many academic studies.In the 1960s, Toyota took advantage of a rapidly growing Japanese economy to sell cars to a growing middle-class, leading to the development of the [Toyota Corolla](:Toyota_Corolla), which would go on to become [the world's all-time best-selling automobile](:List_of_best-selling_automobiles). The booming economy also funded an international expansion that would allow Toyota to grow into one of the [largest automakers in the world](:List_of_manufacturers_by_motor_vehicle_production), the [largest company in Japan](:List_of_largest_Japanese_companies) and the [ninth-largest company in the world by revenue](:List_of_largest_companies_by_revenue), as of December 2020[[update]](//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Toyota&action=edit). Toyota was the world's first automobile manufacturer to produce more than 10 million vehicles per year, a record set in 2012, when it also reported the production of its 200 millionth vehicle.Toyota was praised for being a leader in the development and sales of more fuel-efficient [hybrid electric vehicles](:Hybrid_electric_vehicle), starting with the introduction of the [Toyota Prius](:Toyota_Prius) in 1997. The company now sells more than 40 hybrid vehicle models around the world. However, more recently, the company has also been accused of [greenwashing](:Greenwashing) for its skepticism of [all-electric vehicles](:Electric_vehicle) and its focus on the development of [hydrogen fuel cell vehicles](:Fuel_cell_vehicle), like the [Toyota Mirai](:Toyota_Mirai), a technology that is costlier and has fallen far behind electric batteries.As of 2022[[update]](//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Toyota&action=edit), the Toyota Motor Corporation produces vehicles under four brands: [Daihatsu](:Daihatsu), [Hino](:Hino_Motors), [Lexus](:Lexus) and the namesake Toyota. The company also holds a 20% stake in [Subaru Corporation](:Subaru_Corporation), a 5.1% stake in [Mazda](:Mazda), a 4.9% stake in [Suzuki](:Suzuki), a 4.6% stake in [Isuzu](:Isuzu), a 3.8% stake in [Yamaha Motor Corporation](:Yamaha_Motor_Corporation), and a 2.8% stake in [Panasonic](:Panasonic), as well as stakes in vehicle manufacturing joint-ventures in China ([FAW Toyota](:FAW_Toyota) and [GAC Toyota](:GAC_Toyota%29), the Czech Republic ([TPCA](:Toyota_Peugeot_Citro%C3%ABn_Automobile_Czech%29), India ([Toyota Kirloskar](:Toyota_Kirloskar_Motor%29) and the United States ([MTMUS](:Mazda_Toyota_Manufacturing_USA%29).Toyota is listed on the [London Stock Exchange](:London_Stock_Exchange), [Nagoya Stock Exchange](:Nagoya_Stock_Exchange), [New York Stock Exchange](:New_York_Stock_Exchange) and on the [Tokyo Stock Exchange](:Tokyo_Stock_Exchange), where its stock is a component of the [Nikkei 225](:Nikkei_225) and [TOPIX](:TOPIX) Core30 indices."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
