<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Åram_Church> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Åram Church** (Template:Lang-no is a [parish church](:Parish_church) of the [Church of Norway](:Church_of_Norway) in the [municipality](:List_of_municipalities_of_Norway) of [Vanylven](:Vanylven) in [Møre og Romsdal](:M%C3%B8re_og_Romsdal) county, [Norway](:Norway). It is located in the village of [Åram](:%C3%85ram) in the northern part of the municipality. It is the church for the Åram [parish](:Parish) which is part of the [Søre Sunnmøre prosti](:S%C3%B8re_Sunnm%C3%B8re_prosti) ([deanery](:Deanery%29) in the [Diocese of Møre](:Diocese_of_M%C3%B8re) (since 2002; prior to that time it was part of the [Sande](:Sande%2C_M%C3%B8re_og_Romsdal) parish). The white, wooden church was built in a [long church](:Long_church) design in 1927 using plans drawn up by the [architect](:Architect) Sivert Storegjerde. The church seats about 300 people."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
