<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Leavenworth,_Kansas> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Leavenworth** () is the [county seat](:County_seat) and largest [city](:City) of [Leavenworth County](:Leavenworth_County%2C_Kansas), [Kansas](:Kansas), [United States](:United_States) and is part of the [Kansas City metropolitan area](:Kansas_City_metropolitan_area). As of the [2020 census](:2020_United_States_census), the population of the city was 37,351. It is located on the west bank of the [Missouri River](:Missouri_River). The site of [Fort Leavenworth](:Fort_Leavenworth), built in 1827, the city became known in [American history](:History_of_the_United_States) for its role as a key supply base in the settlement of the [American West](:American_frontier). During the American Civil War, many volunteers joined the Union Army from Leavenworth. The city has been notable as the location of several prisons, particularly the [United States Disciplinary Barracks](:United_States_Disciplinary_Barracks) and [United States Penitentiary, Leavenworth](:United_States_Penitentiary%2C_Leavenworth)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
