<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Cheshire> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Cheshire, archaically known as the County Palatine of Chester, is both a ceremonial and historic county (with differing boundaries for each) in northwest England. It is bordered by Wales to the west and the English counties of Merseyside and Greater Manchester to the north, Derbyshire to the east, and Staffordshire and Shropshire to the south. Cheshire's county town is the cathedral city of Chester, while its largest town by population is Warrington. Other towns in the county include Alsager, Congleton, Crewe, Ellesmere Port, Frodsham, Knutsford, Macclesfield, Middlewich, Nantwich, Neston, Northwich, Poynton, Runcorn, Sandbach, Widnes, Wilmslow, and Winsford."@en .
