<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asheville,_North_Carolina> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Asheville** ( [*ASH-vil*](:Help%3APronunciation_respelling_key%29) is a city in, and the [county seat](:County_seat) of, [Buncombe County, North Carolina](:Buncombe_County%2C_North_Carolina), United States. Located at the confluence of the [French Broad](:French_Broad_River) and [Swannanoa](:Swannanoa_River) rivers, it is the largest city in [Western North Carolina](:Western_North_Carolina), and the state's [11th-most populous city](:List_of_municipalities_in_North_Carolina). According to the [2020 United States Census](:2020_United_States_Census), the city's population was 94,589, up from 83,393 in the 2010 census. It is the principal city in the four-county [Asheville metropolitan area](:Asheville_metropolitan_area), which had a population of 424,858 in 2010, and of 469,015 in 2020."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
