<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Cleveland_Charge> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Cleveland Charge** are an American professional [basketball](:Basketball) team in the [NBA G League](:NBA_G_League) based in [Cleveland, Ohio](:Cleveland%2C_Ohio), and are affiliated with the [Cleveland Cavaliers](:Cleveland_Cavaliers). The team plays its home games at the [Wolstein Center](:Wolstein_Center) in downtown Cleveland.The franchise was founded in 2001 as the **Huntsville Flight**, based in [Huntsville, Alabama](:Huntsville%2C_Alabama), before moving to [Albuquerque, New Mexico](:Albuquerque%2C_New_Mexico) in 2005, where they were known as the **Albuquerque Thunderbirds** until 2010. After playing the 2010–11 season in suburban [Rio Rancho](:Rio_Rancho%2C_New_Mexico) as the **New Mexico Thunderbirds**, the franchise was purchased by the Cavaliers and relocated to [Canton, Ohio](:Canton%2C_Ohio), where they played as the **Canton Charge** through the 2020–21 season.The team won the 2006 NBA D-League championship while playing in Albuquerque. The team lost the 2003–04 NBA D-League Finals, and reached the semifinals in 2004–05, 2006–07, 2011–12, 2014–15 and 2015–16."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
