<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Monroe,_Michigan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Monroe** is the largest city and [county seat](:County_seat) of [Monroe County](:Monroe_County%2C_Michigan) in the U.S. state of [Michigan](:Michigan). Monroe had a population of 20,462 in the [2020 census](:2020_United_States_Census). The city is bordered on the south by [Monroe Charter Township](:Monroe_Charter_Township%2C_Michigan), but the two are administered autonomously. Monroe is the core city in the [Monroe metropolitan statistical area](:List_of_metropolitan_statistical_areas), which is coterminous with Monroe County and had a population of 154,809 in 2020. Located on the western shores of [Lake Erie](:Lake_Erie) approximately 14 miles (23 km) north of [Toledo, Ohio](:Toledo%2C_Ohio) and 25 miles (40 km) south of [Detroit](:Detroit), the city is part of the [Detroit–Ann Arbor–Flint](:Metro_Detroit) combined statistical area.The Monroe area was the scene of several military conflicts during the [War of 1812](:War_of_1812) against the [United Kingdom](:United_Kingdom_of_Great_Britain_and_Ireland) and is known for the [Battle of Frenchtown](:Battle_of_Frenchtown). In 1817, portions of the [Frenchtown](:Frenchtown_Charter_Township%2C_Michigan) settlement along the [River Raisin](:River_Raisin) were [platted](:Plat) and renamed Monroe after then-president [James Monroe](:James_Monroe). When Michigan became a state in 1837, Monroe was incorporated as a city.Monroe is known as the childhood residence of [George Armstrong Custer](:George_Armstrong_Custer) and other members of his family, including his brother [Boston Custer](:Boston_Custer) and wife [Elizabeth Bacon](:Elizabeth_Bacon_Custer). Several structures are named after Custer, including [Custer Airport](:Custer_Airport). Founded in 1928, the [La-Z-Boy](:La-Z-Boy) world headquarters are located in Monroe."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
