<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Leaning_Tower_of_Teluk_Intan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Leaning Tower of Teluk Intan (Malay: Menara Jam Condong Teluk Intan) is a clock and a leaning tower in Teluk Intan, Hilir Perak District, Perak, Malaysia. It is the Malaysian equivalent of the Leaning Tower of Pisa. It is 25 m (82 ft) and, from the outside, looks like an 8 storey building, though inside it is actually divided into 3 storeys."@en .
