<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Providence,_Rhode_Island> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Providence** is the capital and most populous city of the [U.S. state](:U%2ES%2E_state) of [Rhode Island](:Rhode_Island), also the most populous city of [Providence County](:Providence_County). One of the oldest cities in New England, it was founded in 1636 by [Roger Williams](:Roger_Williams), a Reformed Baptist theologian and religious exile from the [Massachusetts Bay Colony](:Massachusetts_Bay_Colony). He named the area in honor of \"God's merciful Providence\" which he believed was responsible for revealing such a haven for him and his followers. The city is situated at the mouth of the [Providence River](:Providence_River) at the head of [Narragansett Bay](:Narragansett_Bay).Providence was one of the first cities in the country to industrialize and became noted for its textile manufacturing and subsequent machine tool, jewelry, and silverware industries. Today, the city of Providence is home to eight hospitals and [eight institutions of higher learning](:List_of_colleges_and_universities_in_Rhode_Island%23Institutions) which have shifted the city's economy into service industries, though it still retains some manufacturing activity.As of the [2020 U.S. census](:2020_United_States_census), Providence has a population of 190,934, making it the third-most-populous city in [New England](:New_England) after [Boston](:Boston) and [Worcester](:Worcester%2C_Massachusetts), Massachusetts."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
