<http://dbpedia.org/resource/University_of_Alberta> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **University of Alberta**, also known as **U of A** or **UAlberta**, is a [public](:Public_university) [research university](:Research_university) located in [Edmonton, Alberta](:Edmonton%2C_Alberta), Canada. It was founded in 1908 by [Alexander Cameron Rutherford](:Alexander_Cameron_Rutherford), the first premier of Alberta, and [Henry Marshall Tory](:Henry_Marshall_Tory), the university's first president. It was enabled through the Post-secondary Learning Act*.*The university is considered a \"comprehensive academic and research university\" (CARU), which means that it offers a range of academic and professional programs that generally lead to undergraduate and graduate level credentials.The university comprises four campuses in Edmonton, an Augustana Campus in [Camrose](:Camrose%2C_Alberta), and a staff centre in downtown [Calgary](:Calgary). The original north campus consists of 150 buildings covering 50 city blocks on the south rim of the [North Saskatchewan River valley](:North_Saskatchewan_River_valley_parks_system), directly across from [downtown Edmonton](:Downtown_Edmonton). 39,000 students from Canada and 150 other countries participate in 400 programs in 18 faculties.The university is a major economic driver in Alberta. Its impact on Alberta's economy is estimated at $12.3 billion annually, or five per cent of the province's gross domestic product."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
